	"reviewNotes": [
		"Hausa is spoken as a second language almost everywhere in the north; only areas where sources name Hausa as a home language are mapped.",
		"In Kebbi and Kaduna the share is inferred from where other peoples are sourced; check the southern Kaduna and southern Kebbi LGAs.",
		"Adamawa and Taraba were not covered by the North East survey and are not yet mapped for Hausa.",
		"Southern Kebbi (Zuru, Sakaba, Wasagu/Danko, Fakai, Yauri, Ngaski, Shanga) is now mapped for its own peoples; the Hausa share there is still inferred."
	],
